//! `@std.grammar` — a generic grammar engine. Declare a grammar as
//! data (`Grammar`/`Rule`/`Alt`/`Seq`/`Item`/`Prim`), write it as DSL
//! text and parse it back (`parse_grammar`), merge same-named rules
//! from independently-authored fragments (`Grammar.merged`), and run
//! it over any tokenizable input (`run_grammar`) — any token type
//! implementing `Lexeme`.
//!
//! Owns no lexer of its own: a token stream in, a `Grammar` or a
//! parsed value out. Avra's own compiler is one caller, driving this
//! engine over its own token type to assemble the language's grammar
//! from its LanguageFeature fragments; any other program tokenizing
//! its own notation the same way can drive it the same one.
